cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use humans-md in research or practice, cite this software and identify the evaluated commit."
title: "humans-md: Portable Behaviour Contracts and Casefile Workflows for Coding Agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "alsi-lawr"
abstract: >-
  humans-md is a vendor-neutral instruction and workflow artifact for
  agent-assisted repository work. It packages portable behaviour contracts,
  task-shaped skills, deterministic validators, and a governed Casefile process
  into reproducible Codex and Claude plugins. The repository also preserves an
  evidenced design and implementation report with explicit verification limits.
version: "0.4.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alsi-lawr/HUMANS.md"
url: "https://github.com/alsi-lawr/HUMANS.md"
keywords:
  - "AI agents"
  - "coding agents"
  - "human-agent interaction"
  - "instruction systems"
  - "research software"
  - "software engineering"
